From 27d762683608dd8fb1ece12ab17e78e54f43c593 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:25:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] carhacks: point tools and docs at bake (formerly d1cars)

bigrig_extract.py looked for the page decoder in MODS/d1cars/tools and silently
skipped the page PNGs; slotmap.py read LCFs from MODS/d1cars/tools/out/lcf. Both
folders are gone since the module became bake: the decoder is in
MODS/bake/tools/car (pages1.py) and the LCFs are written to
MODS/bake/tools/car/out/lcf (bake/tools/car/README.md). The DRIVER1.md links move
to bake/docs. d1citymodels.h still names a gen_d1citymodels.py that no longer
exists in either repo; left as is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015LjSznjzjHgGhjQaMfW1Mq
---
 HANDOFF.md              | 2 +-
 docs/FORMATS.md         | 2 +-
 docs/PALETTES.md        | 2 +-
 tools/bigrig_extract.py | 2 +-
 tools/slotmap.py        | 2 +-
 5 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/HANDOFF.md b/HANDOFF.md
index e0ae89a..bd5c67d 100644
--- a/HANDOFF.md
+++ b/HANDOFF.md
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ detail lives in the topic docs.
    NEWCASTLE blob: model 1 = 75 of 135 polys on set 0, model 2 = 78 of 139, model 3 = 20 of 233
    (only its untextured ones) - the "invisible hood on car 1, cars 1 and 2 half broken, car 3
    fine" report. The bake now numbers from 1 (`PAGE_SET_BASE`) and drops Driver 1's flat
-   untextured polys instead of faking them as textured on set 0. See `d1cars/docs/DRIVER1.md`.
+   untextured polys instead of faking them as textured on set 0. See `bake/docs/DRIVER1.md`.
 
 2. **A palette row the lump cannot fill was FABRICATED** (`cars.c`). The alias copied a
    neighbouring row's six columns including slot 0 - which the draw then accepted as this
diff --git a/docs/FORMATS.md b/docs/FORMATS.md
index 53eaf9b..c1987bd 100644
--- a/docs/FORMATS.md
+++ b/docs/FORMATS.md
@@ -351,7 +351,7 @@ print(total, sets)
   appears once the walk runs *past* `num_polys` (into the next model or other
   data), so the real caveat is to **bound the walk**, not that the stream is
   compressed. Driver 1's car models use the same encoding; see
-  `MODS/d1cars/docs/DRIVER1.md`.
+  `MODS/bake/docs/DRIVER1.md`.
 - City car sets live in the low numbers (**10..68** across all four cities), so set
   indices **110+ are free** and safe to re-index an imported page onto.
 - `LUMP_TEXTUREINFO` (type **34**, DATA1) is **not** "a count then entries". The layout
diff --git a/docs/PALETTES.md b/docs/PALETTES.md
index a5a5eab..90d29eb 100644
--- a/docs/PALETTES.md
+++ b/docs/PALETTES.md
@@ -531,7 +531,7 @@ The row is now left empty and reported. Empty is already handled end to end:
 * `CarClutLookup` falls back to the group's slot 0, never to the framebuffer.
 
 This is only reachable because a bake never numbers a car page 0 any more (see
-`d1cars/docs/DRIVER1.md`): with the sentinel set back, the pin takes every set a model names,
+`bake/docs/DRIVER1.md`): with the sentinel set back, the pin takes every set a model names,
 so slot 0 is always filled. Verified: a RIO level importing CHICAGO model 8 passes all three
 `crosscheck.py` invariants, INV3 included (its CLUT rows still MATCH `CHICAGO.LEV`), and
 `cardump.py` reports those pages as "only the page's own CLUT applies (no leak)".
diff --git a/tools/bigrig_extract.py b/tools/bigrig_extract.py
index d88a88f..787b4aa 100644
--- a/tools/bigrig_extract.py
+++ b/tools/bigrig_extract.py
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
 # The page decoder (decomp_asm + the CLUT unpacking) lives in the Driver 1 car tools,
 # where it was written to read exactly these page entries. Optional: without it the
 # geometry and cosmetics still come out, only the page PNGs are skipped.
-D1_TOOLS = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, "..", "..", "d1cars", "tools"))
+D1_TOOLS = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, "..", "..", "bake", "tools", "car"))
 if os.path.isdir(D1_TOOLS):
     sys.path.insert(0, D1_TOOLS)
 
diff --git a/tools/slotmap.py b/tools/slotmap.py
index 8c478dd..0b8e2de 100644
--- a/tools/slotmap.py
+++ b/tools/slotmap.py
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ import sys
 
 HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
 LCF_DIR = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(
-    HERE, "..", "..", "..", "MODS", "d1cars", "tools", "out", "lcf"))
+    HERE, "..", "..", "..", "MODS", "bake", "tools", "car", "out", "lcf"))
 
 D2_CITIES = ("CHICAGO", "HAVANA", "VEGAS", "RIO")
 # Driver 2's own model numbers - the ones its four cities ship and its frontend
